Per zod@4.5.4:

In zod v4, each item in a `ZodError.issues` array is a `ZodIssue` (aliased to `core.$ZodIssue`) with fields like `expected`, `code`, `path`, and `message` (e.g. `expected: 'string'`, `code: 'invalid_type'`, `path: ['username']`, `message: 'Invalid input: expected string'`). `safeParse` returns a discriminated union: on success `{ success: true; data }`, on failure `{ success: false; error: ZodError }`. To get the issues on failure, check `!result.success` then read `result.error.issues` (or access `err.issues` after catching a `ZodError` thrown by `parse`).

Source excerpt:
> ```ts
> const result = Player.safeParse({ username: 42, xp: "100" });
> if (!result.success) {
>   result.error; // ZodError instance
> } else {
>   result.data; // { username: string; xp: number }
> }
> ```

